/ref 17592186416683 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416685 1069 "q-278253" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416685 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416685 1071 "![](images/1a/1a8e0f0c766d2674dbf32feac760baea28418d65565fd6d64dccc6cf3eecd6bf.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416685 1072 #uuid "d94a5264-18c5-5679-b580-fde7816b3b57" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416685 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-3,4),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416686 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416684 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416686 1069 "q-7630" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416686 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416686 1071 "![](images/e2/e2cabfed6c7008b47c3157cca4862d0c2a5b2a2b34e1bb35aeea963b1639af8c.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416686 1072 #uuid "ee934c99-4f27-5203-a0f5-c13e99354b00" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416686 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=1,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416687 1062 #uuid "036e2b13-48e5-5f1c-9ff0-5814ddca4cfd" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416687 1063 #edb/ref 17592186372489 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416688 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416690 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416688 1062 #uuid "af068651-d4d2-5cf0-9c59-16a00c0246fe" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416688 1063 #edb/ref 17592186416686 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416689 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416687 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416689 1062 #uuid "bfc51aac-6584-5b70-b332-8fd371dd660d" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416689 1063 #edb/ref 17592186416685 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416690 1058 #edb/ref 17592186416689 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416690 1062 #uuid "f12ab8ea-ca60-5bc7-a665-f8bdd2c2c872" 13194139534270 17592186045417 true] [17592186416690 1063 #edb/ref 17592186250388 13194139534270 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-4e7ed6bf-1bc2-544f-a2b2-ce9a57e934dc" 17592186416676 "answer-06b57d90-a9ee-54f9-840f-6dfdd3aab51c" 17592186416677 "answer-23962a06-bb97-5fbd-a080-34dac0fedadd" 17592186416678 "answer-3c3d7e26-2073-5af5-a3f5-d42d26f20154" 17592186416679 "answer-4376677f-9a7f-532f-b66b-ad4902b9c630" 17592186416680 "answer-b2919188-309d-5e3e-965d-f1e83d98bddc" 17592186416681 "answer-d9e0ee02-13c6-544f-b4b9-39031730f3ff" 17592186416682 "answer-field-43d267b9-ec22-5b8b-a0c1-af357d98c1d6" 17592186416683 "answer-field-759f0728-d8d2-515a-b991-0560a3f812fb" 17592186416684 "question-d94a5264-18c5-5679-b580-fde7816b3b57" 175